Toggle Chips for selecting multiple peer filters"},"295":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-30","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#features","content":"Removable Chips for user-added filters and input tokens"},"296":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-31","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#features","content":"Shared `sm`, `md`, and `lg` sizes, with optional leading icons"},"297":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-32","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#features","content":"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"},"298":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-33","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#default","content":"Start with a labeled group of related values. Add selection or removal when\nthe group needs interactive behavior."},"299":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-34","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#toggle-chips","content":"Use Toggle Chips for multiple peer filters. Selected items show a check while\nunselected items remain available in the same group."},"300":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-35","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#removable-chips","content":"Use Removable Chips for user-added filters and tokens. Removing a Chip calls\nthe group callback so the owning collection can update its items."},"301":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-36","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#controlled-selection","content":"Use `selectedKeys` and `onSelectionChange` when another part of the page\nneeds to own the selected filter state."},"302":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-37","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#sizes","content":"Compare the supported `sm`, `md`, and `lg` sizes. Keep one size per group."},"303":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-38","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#disabled","content":"Disable individual options with `disabledKeys` when some values are unavailable."},"304":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-39","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#truncation","content":"By default, long labels truncate visually when space is constrained, while\nthe complete accessible value remains available."},"305":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-40","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#empty-state","content":"Give an empty collection useful guidance, then let the user add the first\nvalue. Removable items continue to be owned by the collection."},"306":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-41","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#menu-filter-trigger","content":"Use `ChipButton` for a menu trigger that shares the Chip family's compact\nsizing and presentation."},"307":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-42","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#customization","content":"Use a plain string for a simple Chip label. When content is composed, use\n`Text` for the visible label and `textValue` for the complete accessible value."},"308":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-43","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#customization","content":"Set the size on `ChipGroup` to share it with every Chip. `ChipList` wraps items\nhorizontally by default, and its layout props can be customized when needed."},"309":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-44","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#customization","content":"For removable Chips, provide `onRemove` on the group and add a self-closing\n`Button` with `slot=\"remove\"`. The callback receives a `Set` of removed keys;\nupdate the collection owned by your application."},"310":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-45","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#customization","content":"For Toggle Chips, use the Chip render prop to show a selected accessory."},"311":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-46","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#menu-filter-button","content":"When you need a menu with a Chip-like appearance, use `ChipButton` inside\n`MenuTrigger`. The menu trigger owns open state, focus, keyboard interaction,\nand `aria-expanded`; the consumer owns any configured-filter state."},"312":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-47","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Use `Label` or `aria-label` to name the `ChipGroup`; this names the collection,\nnot its individual Chips."},"313":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-48","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Give each Chip a visible label, `textValue`, or `aria-label`. Use `textValue`\nwhen a Chip contains icons, composed content, or a render prop."},"314":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-49","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Use a descriptive group label so removal actions can be announced clearly."},"315":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-50","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Keep the visible label and the accessible value synchronized."},"316":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-51","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."},"317":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-52","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Keep labels concise and let them truncate only when the available width requires it."},"318":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-53","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Prefer groups of three or more related values."},"319":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-54","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Keep one size per group."},"320":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-55","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Let `ChipList` wrap instead of forcing a single horizontal line."},"321":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-56","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Use removable Chips for user-added filters and tokens."},"322":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-57","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"For menu filters, use `ChipButton` with `MenuTrigger` and provide the chevron explicitly."},"323":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-58","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#a-chipgroup-has-no-accessible-name","content":"Add a visible `Label` to the group or provide `aria-label`. For an individual Chip\nwith composed content, provide a visible label, `textValue`, or `aria-label`."},"324":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-59","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#the-remove-action-does-not-update-the-ui","content":"Add `onRemove` to `ChipGroup` and remove the returned keys from the collection\nowned by your application."},"325":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-60","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#a-composed-label-is-not-truncating-correctly","content":"Keep the label in `Text`, preserve `textValue`, and constrain the available width\nof the surrounding layout. Truncation is visual; the complete accessible value\nshould remain available."},"326":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-61","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#the-menu-trigger-does-not-look-like-a-chip","content":"Use `ChipButton` inside `MenuTrigger`, include the visible value, and add a\ntrailing chevron to communicate that the control opens a menu."},"327":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-62","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#props","content":"For a menu trigger, the button and menu are composed as siblings inside\n`MenuTrigger`:"},"328":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"page","content":"CircularProgress","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress"},"329":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-0","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress","content":"A circular progress indicator shows determinate progress of an operation over time"},"330":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-1","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#installation","content":"Installation"},"331":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-2","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#examples","content":"Examples"},"332":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-3","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#default","content":"Default"},"333":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-4","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"334":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-5","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#emphasis","content":"Emphasis"},"335":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-6","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"336":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-7","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"337":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-8","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#props","content":"Props"},"338":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-9","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#default","content":"A basic determinate progress indicator with a label and helper text."},"339":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-10","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#sizes","content":"Four circle diameters are available: `sm` (64px), `md` (96px), `lg` (128px), and `xl` (160px)."},"340":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-11","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#emphasis","content":"Use the `emphasis` prop to communicate status: `success`, `warning`, or `critical`. When omitted, the default teal fill is used."},"341":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-12","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#aria-support","content":"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the