ce"],[316,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[293,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[1528,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[1738,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1212,"`Content`, `Header`, `Footer`, and `ButtonGroup` each accept all `Flex` layout props."],[961,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[566,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[569,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[565,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[567,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[568,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[570,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1253,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[366,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[399,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[875,"`Enter/Space`"],[451,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[657,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[408,"`Escape`"],[803,"`Escape`"],[877,"`Escape`"],[1533,"`Escape`"],[487,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1806,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[574,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1844,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[470,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[645,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[674,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[1721,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[1775,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[700,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1774,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[735,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[147,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[369,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[798,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[794,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[960,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1581,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1323,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1523,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[665,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[648,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[869,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[651,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[904,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[909,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1015,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[1740,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[1741,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[1739,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[805,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[879,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[412,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[573,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[572,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[341,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[925,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1025,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1149,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1024,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1148,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1487,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1486,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[741,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once